                <pb facs="0927" n="825" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg825"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/645: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jefferson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-27T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27, 1919,
                                11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 28,
                            1.20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Information received yesterday is to the effect that the Acosta force of 300 men
                    attacked 800 of Tinoco forces at El Jobo near Liberia. It seems that the battle
                    lasted five hours. Losses were sustained on both sides. The Acosta force retired
                    to their base of operations on account of shortage in ammunition. It is reported
                    that Tinoco has in the vicinity of Guanacaste a force of approximately 2,000 men
                    well equipped and fortified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
